      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Proposition 2.2. Let V = {0} be an ordered normed space whose cone has an interior",
      "kids" : [ {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 1,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 716.053, 510.232, 740.533 ],
        "font" : "SFTI1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "point v. Then v is an order unit and the order unit norm   · v is weaker than the original norm   ·  on V . Moreover, every positive functional on V is continuous with respect to"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 2,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 702.493, 140.832, 713.413 ],
        "font" : "SFTI1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "both norms."
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 3,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 666.493, 510.093, 692.751 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Note that the two norms in Proposition 2.2 need not be equivalent, see, e.g., [6, Example 1.5.12]. For a detailed discussion in ordered Banach spaces, see [4, Proposition 2.11]."
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 4,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 85.079, 612.253, 510.265, 665.631 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "For an ordered vector space (V,V+), a set S′ of positive linear functionals from V to R is said to determine positivity if, for every v ∈ V , one has v ≥ 0 if ϕ(v) ≥ 0 for all ϕ ∈ S′. Note that, if V is an order unit space and Σ ⊆ V+′ is given as in (2.1), then ext Σ determines positivity."
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 5,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 101.999, 598.692, 379.841, 611.391 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "We will make use of the following two simple propositions."
      } ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 85.079, 562.692, 510.405, 588.918 ],
      "font" : "SFBX1095",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Proposition 2.3. Let X be an ordered normed vector space and let S′ ⊆ X+′ . The following are equivalent:",
      "kids" : [ {
        "type" : "list",
        "pdfua_tag" : "L",
        "id" : 6,
        "level" : "2",
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 92.399, 503.271, 510.234, 552.831 ],
        "numbering style" : "roman numbers",
        "number of list items" : 2,
        "list items" : [ {
          "type" : "list item",
          "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
          "page number" : 1,
          "bounding box" : [ 95.399, 526.572, 510.234, 552.831 ],
          "font" : "SFRM1095",
          "font size" : 10.909,
          "text color" : "[0.0]",
          "content" : "(i) The set S′ determines positivity, i.e., for every x ∈ X, the inequality x′,x ≥ 0 for all x′ ∈ S′ implies that x ≥ 0.",
          "kids" : [ ]
        }, {
          "type" : "list item",
          "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
          "page number" : 1,
          "bounding box" : [ 92.399, 503.271, 433.995, 516.711 ],
          "font" : "SFRM1095",
          "font size" : 10.909,
          "text color" : "[0.0]",
          "content" : "(ii) The positive-linear hull of S′ is weak-∗ dense in the dual wedge X+′ .",
          "kids" : [ ]
        } ]
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 7,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 85.079, 399.231, 510.195, 494.271 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Proof. “(i) ⇒ (ii)” We show the contraposition. Let C′ ⊆ X+′ denote the weak-∗ closure of the positive-linear hull of S′ and assume that there exists a point x′0 ∈ X+′ that is not in C′. By the Hahn–Banach separation theorem in the locally convex space X′ with the weak-∗ topology, there exists a weak-∗ continuous functional x′′: X′ → R and a number γ ∈ R such that x′′,x′ ≥ γ > x′′,x′0 for all x′ ∈ C′. Due to the weak-∗ continuity of x′′, there exists an element x ∈ X such that x′′ is the point evaluation at x, see [13, § IV.1.2 on pp.124–125]. It follows that x,x′ ≥ γ > x,x′0"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 8,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 112.319, 373.212, 510.254, 399.35 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "for all x′ ∈ C′. Since 0 ∈ C′, we obtain γ ≤ 0. Therefore, x is not in X+. As C′ is a wedge, for every x′ ∈ C′ we have x,x′ ≥ 0, hence C′ does not determine positivity."
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 9,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 85.079, 314.533, 510.215, 363.35 ],
        "font" : "SFRM1095",
        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "“(ii) ⇒ (i)” If x ∈ X satisﬁes x′,x ≥ 0 for all x′ ∈ S′, then it follows from (ii) that the same inequality holds for all x′ ∈ X+′ . As X+ is closed, this implies that x ∈ X+. The following is a primal version of Proposition 2.3. As its proof is similar, we omit it."
      }, {
